abstract: >-
  Code, per-fold outputs and derived results for the preprint "Decomposing the Performance
  Gains of Pre-Split Resampling in Imbalanced Credit Risk Modelling". The analysis decomposes
  the gap between resampling after and before the
  train-test split into training-side leakage, synthetic-test mixture and prevalence
  contributions that add up exactly to the total in every fold, across six OpenML datasets,
  four models, three resamplers and 30 seeds.
